\title{Multiplicity at a fixed label}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The spinor time map can take a translation block to another block (\ref{fdip-0186}). At a label fixed by such a map, conjugate linearity keeps a real spectral value unchanged. What does the square of the map imply about the number of independent vectors at that value?}
